  "provenance": "UNOFFICIAL third-party mirror of a DLD Ejari export, 6,585,210 registered tenancy contracts. Contract volume is substantial through 2023; 2024 is partial (22,913 contracts) and is excluded. A handful of rows carry implausible years (2107+) and are discarded.",
  "period": "2008–2023",
  "minContracts": 50,
  "method": "Share of registered residential tenancy contracts in the community flagged is_free_hold = 1, across all years held in the export.",
  "limitation": "Derived from TENANCY records, so it reflects the freehold share of rented homes in a community rather than an official designation of the community's land status. Use it as a strong indicator of where non-GCC buyers can purchase, not as legal confirmation for a specific plot. Dubai land law makes this effectively BIMODAL: a community is either freehold or it is not, so about half of scored communities sit at 0% and most of the rest near 100%, and the map reads as two tones rather than a gradient. That is the shape of the underlying law, not a broken colour scale.",
